      "name": "SaveVideoSettingsToRegistry",
      "signature": "void SaveVideoSettingsToRegistry(uint dwRenderMode, int nVideoModeIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Saves video/render settings to the Windows registry under both HKCU and HKLM.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Format registry value name strings for DeviceName, dwFlags, and GUID\n2. Open/create registry key under HKEY_CURRENT_USER\\SOFTWARE\\Blizzard Entertainment\\...\n3. Write render mode (DWORD), device name (string), flags (DWORD), and GUID (binary) values\n4. Close HKCU key handle\n5. Open/create registry key under HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Blizzard Entertainment\\...\n6. Write same set of values to HKLM\n7. Close HKLM key handle\n\nParameters:\n  dwRenderMode (ECX) - Render mode identifier (REG_DWORD value for \"Render\" key)\n  nVideoModeIndex (EDX) - Index into g_VideoModes array (stride 0x48/72 bytes)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value; registry operations may silently fail\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If RegCreateKeyExA fails, skips writing values for that hive\n  - Writes to both HKCU (0x80000001) and HKLM (0x80000002)\n  - GUID value written as REG_BINARY (type 3), 16 bytes\n\nStructure Layout (VideoMode at 0x414aac, stride 72 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field         Description\n  0x00    4     dwFlags       Video mode flags (REG_DWORD)\n  0x04    16    guidDevice    Device GUID (REG_BINARY)\n  0x1C    28    szDeviceName  Device name string (REG_SZ)",
