      "name": "SaveVideoDeviceToRegistry",
      "signature": "void SaveVideoDeviceToRegistry(int nDeviceIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Saves video device configuration to the Windows registry for a specific device index.\n\nWrites the device settings to both HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE and HKEY_CURRENT_USER under:\n  SOFTWARE\\Blizzard Entertainment\\Diablo II\\VideoConfig\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Format registry value names with device index (DeviceName%d, dwFlags%d, GUID%d, Recommend%d)\n2. Calculate device structure offset: index * 288 (0x120) bytes from g_VideoDevices base\n3. Open/create HKLM\\...\\VideoConfig key with KEY_ALL_ACCESS (0x20006)\n4. Write device name as REG_SZ string\n5. Write dwFlags as REG_DWORD\n6. Write GUID as REG_BINARY (16 bytes)\n7. Write Recommend setting as REG_SZ\n8. Close HKLM key\n9. Open/create HKCU\\...\\VideoConfig key\n10. Write same four values to HKCU\n11. Close HKCU key\n\nParameters:\n  nDeviceIndex (ECX): Zero-based index of video device in g_VideoDevices array\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value; errors silently ignored\n\nRegistry Values Written:\n  DeviceName%d - REG_SZ - Device display name from structure offset +0x1C\n  dwFlags%d    - REG_DWORD - Device capability flags from offset +0x00\n  GUID%d       - REG_BINARY (16 bytes) - DirectDraw device GUID from offset +0x04\n  Recommend%d  - REG_SZ - Recommendation string from offset +0x11C\n\nStructure Layout (VideoDeviceInfo at 0x414a90):\n  Offset  Size  Field         Type\n  0x00    4     dwFlags       DWORD\n  0x04    16    guid          GUID\n  0x14    8     reserved      BYTE[8]\n  0x1C    256   szDeviceName  CHAR[256]\n  0x11C   4     dwRecommend   DWORD\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x80000002 - HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\n  0x80000001 - HKEY_CURRENT_USER\n  0x20006    - KEY_ALL_ACCESS (KEY_READ | KEY_WRITE)\n  0x120 (288)- Size of each video device structure entry",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:94a5ef0f30ebb9f800ca355189ed35b5fbd4a792f32d334310ecd9f62eff7860",
