      "name": "LoadVideoDeviceSettingsFromRegistry",
      "signature": "int LoadVideoDeviceSettingsFromRegistry(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Loads video device settings from the Windows registry for all video devices.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize device index counter and recommended flag to 0\n2. For each video device slot (0 to max at 0x41514c):\n   a. Format registry value names: DeviceName%d, dwFlags%d, GUID%d, Recommend%d\n   b. Try opening HKEY_CURRENT_USER\\SOFTWARE\\Blizzard Entertainment\\...\n   c. If successful, read DeviceName, dwFlags, Recommend, and GUID values\n   d. If Recommend value equals 2, mark device as recommended\n   e. Close registry key\n   f. If no recommended device found yet, try HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE as fallback\n   g. Read same values from HKLM if HKCU failed\n   h. Close registry key and advance to next device slot (stride 0x120 bytes)\n3. Return 1 if a recommended device was found, 0 otherwise\n\nParameters:\n  None - This function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\n  int - 1 if a device with Recommend=2 was found, 0 otherwise\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x104 (260) - MAX_PATH, buffer size for registry string values\n  0x20019 - KEY_READ access rights (KEY_QUERY_VALUE | KEY_ENUMERATE_SUB_KEYS | KEY_NOTIFY)\n  0x80000001 - HKEY_CURRENT_USER\n  0x80000002 - HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\n  0x120 (288) - Video device structure stride in global array\n  2 - Recommend flag value indicating recommended device\n\nCalled By:\n  HandlePasswordDialogProc, RunVideoTest",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:c1c7f0b6a96cf98a82665ea014e238e50e5152ed32466b2cc05b4389aba6df9c",
