      "name": "HandleCrashDialogProc",
      "signature": "int HandleCrashDialogProc(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Dialog procedure for the crash/error information dialog.\nShows optional graphics test checkboxes and crash information.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x2108 bytes of stack space for local string buffers\n2. Check message type:\n   - WM_INITDIALOG (0x110): Initialize dialog controls\n   - WM_COMMAND (0x111): Process button commands\n3. For WM_INITDIALOG:\n   a. Load localized dialog title from resource ID 0x20\n   b. Set dialog title with SetWindowTextA\n   c. Show DDraw checkbox (0x3F9) if lpData_00415048 == 1, else hide\n   d. Show D3D checkbox (0x3FA) if lpData_00418070 == 1, else hide\n   e. Show GLIDE checkbox (0x3FB) if lpData_00415038 == 1, else hide\n   f. Load crash info template from resource ID 0x21\n   g. Format crash message with Fog state information\n   h. Set crash info text in control 0x3FC\n   i. Bring dialog to foreground using multiple focus methods\n4. For WM_COMMAND with IDOK (wParam low-word == 1):\n   a. Check each test checkbox state using BM_GETCHECK (0xF2)\n   b. If DDraw checkbox is checked, save to registry TestDDraw value\n   c. If D3D checkbox is checked, save to registry TestD3D value\n   d. If GLIDE checkbox is checked, save to registry TestGLIDE value\n   e. Log completion and close dialog with EndDialog(hDlg, IDOK)\n\nParameters:\n  pDlg (void*) - Handle to the dialog window (HWND)\n  dwMessage (uint) - Windows message identifier\n  dwWParam (uint) - Message-specific parameter (low-word is control ID for WM_COMMAND)\n  nLParam (int) - Message-specific parameter (unused in this function)\n\nReturns:\n  1 (TRUE) - Message was handled successfully\n  0 (FALSE) - Message was not processed (unhandled message types)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x110 - WM_INITDIALOG message\n  0x111 - WM_COMMAND message\n  0x3F9 - DDraw test checkbox control ID\n  0x3FA - D3D test checkbox control ID\n  0x3FB - GLIDE test checkbox control ID\n  0x3FC - Crash info text control ID\n  0xF2 - BM_GETCHECK message\n  0x20 - Dialog title string resource ID\n  0x21 - Crash info template string resource ID\n  0x80000001 - HKEY_CURRENT_USER registry hive\n  0xF003F - KEY_ALL_ACCESS registry access rights",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04c",
