      "name": "EnumerateDisplayAdapters",
      "signature": "int EnumerateDisplayAdapters(HINSTANCE hInstance)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Enumerates DirectDraw/Direct3D display adapters for video testing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check Windows NT version - versions < 5.0 don't support D3D acceleration\n2. Log detection start message\n3. Create hidden enumeration window (640x480, WS_POPUP | WS_DISABLED)\n4. Call DirectDrawEnumerateA with EnumerateDisplayAdapter callback\n5. If enumeration fails, log error via FUN_00405370 and cleanup\n6. Destroy enumeration window on success\n7. Check if any valid D3D devices were found\n8. Return result based on OS version and device capabilities\n\nParameters:\n  hInstance - Application instance handle for window creation\n\nReturns:\n  0 - Failure (NT < 5.0, window creation failed, or no devices found)\n  1 - Success with standard capabilities\n  2 - Success with enhanced capabilities (device meets threshold)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Windows NT < 5.0: Immediately returns 0 (no D3D support)\n  - Window creation failure: Logs error with GetLastError result\n\nGlobals Modified:\n  DWORD_0041880c - Device count (reset to 0 before enumeration)\n  DWORD_00418808 - Enumeration window handle\n  DWORD_00418810 - Device capability value (compared against threshold)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:4babea50f58ec5481c889a9ffa2d96ab",
