      "name": "CleanupD3DEnumerationAndEvaluateResult",
      "signature": "int CleanupD3DEnumerationAndEvaluateResult(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Cleans up D3D enumeration window and evaluates device capability result.\n\nThis function is a shared epilogue block called from EnumerateDisplayAdapters\nafter DirectDraw enumeration completes (whether successful or failed).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if enumeration window exists (DWORD_00418808 != 0)\n2. If window exists, destroy it via DestroyWindow and log message\n3. Check if any valid D3D devices were found (DWORD_0041880c)\n4. If no devices found, log error and return 0 (failure)\n5. Compare device capability (pFogState+0xc) against threshold g_adwData_40f1ec[3]\n6. If below threshold, return 1 (standard capability)\n7. Compare global DWORD_00418810 against threshold g_adwData_40f1ec[2]\n8. Return 2 if meets enhanced threshold, otherwise return 1\n\nParameters:\n  None (uses inherited register context from caller):\n    IMPLICIT dwZero (EBX) - Zero constant for comparison\n    IMPLICIT pFogState (EDI) - Pointer to fog/system state structure\n    IMPLICIT pCallerFrame (EBP) - Caller's stack frame pointer\n\nReturns:\n  0 - Failure (no valid D3D devices found)\n  1 - Success with standard device capabilities\n  2 - Success with enhanced device capabilities (meets higher threshold)\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n  DWORD_00418808 - D3D enumeration window handle\n  DWORD_0041880c - Valid D3D device count\n  DWORD_00418810 - Device capability value\n  g_adwData_40f1ec - Capability threshold array (floats at indices 2,3)\n\nSSA Temporaries (decompiler-generated, cannot be renamed):\n  uVar1/dVar1 (uint) - dwDeviceCapability: Device capability from pFogState+0xc\n  dVar2 (uint) - dwDeviceValue: Value from DWORD_00418810 for comparison\n  iVar2/iVar3 (int) - nResultCode: Return value (1 or 2)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "STR",
