      "name": "CheckTextureFormat1555Support",
      "signature": "int CheckTextureFormat1555Support(int nPixelFormat, uint * pdwCapabilityFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Checks if a texture format descriptor matches 1555 ARGB format requirements.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Return early with success (1) if output flags pointer is NULL\n2. Compare 6 DWORD fields from pixel format structure against reference values:\n   - Offset +0x04: dwFlags (DWORD_0041185c)\n   - Offset +0x0C: dwRBitMask (DWORD_00411864)\n   - Offset +0x10: dwGBitMask (DWORD_00411868)\n   - Offset +0x14: dwBBitMask (DWORD_0041186c)\n   - Offset +0x18: dwRGBAlphaBitMask (DWORD_00411870)\n   - Offset +0x1C: Reserved (DWORD_00411874)\n3. If ALL fields match, set bit 9 (0x200) in capability flags via OR operation\n4. Return success (1) unconditionally\n\nParameters:\n    pPixelFormat - Pointer to DDPIXELFORMAT structure describing texture format\n    pdwCapabilityFlags - Output pointer to adapter capability flags (bit 9 = 1555 support)\n\nReturns:\n    1 - Always returns success\n\nCalled By:\n    EnumerateDisplayAdapter via IDirect3DDevice::EnumTextureFormats callback\n\nNotes:\n    This is a callback function for D3D texture format enumeration.\n    The 1555 format check enables 16-bit textures with 1-bit alpha channel.",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:1c77854589d16599ee882d4b85f6e763abe41fc0477a62025e6de045f8f6fc82",
