      "name": "TestDirectDrawDeviceCapabilities",
      "signature": "dword TestDirectDrawDeviceCapabilities(GUID * pGuid, dword dwUnused, char * szDeviceName)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Tests DirectDraw device capabilities and validates display modes for Diablo II video requirements.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if maximum display card count (2) already reached; return 0 if exceeded\n2. Initialize device data array at index [DWORD_00418f6c * 0xe8]\n3. Store GUID if provided, otherwise mark as primary display (null GUID)\n4. Create DirectDraw object via DirectDrawCreate\n5. If not using secondary monitor (DWORD_00418f58 == 0), query DirectDraw7 interface\n6. Copy device name to device data array and log \"Checking capabilities\"\n7. Set cooperative level (DDSCL_NORMAL = 0x11)\n8. Enumerate display modes, storing results in device data array\n9. Loop through enumerated modes checking for bit depth support\n10. Set capability flags based on best available color depth\n11. Get DirectDraw capabilities (GetCaps) and check for hardware features\n12. Store total/free video memory in device data array\n13. Copy complete device info to primary or secondary device storage\n14. Increment device counter and log success message\n15. Clean up DirectDraw interfaces on exit\n\nParameters:\n  pGuid: Pointer to device GUID (NULL for primary display adapter)\n  dwUnused: Reserved parameter from DirectDraw enumeration callback (not used)\n  szDeviceName: Device name string from enumeration callback\n\nReturns:\n  0: Error occurred (exceeded device limit or DirectDraw failure)\n  1: Success but no more processing needed\n  Result of FUN_00404fb8: Success with continued processing\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Maximum 2 devices supported (DWORD_00418f6c tracks count)\n  - Primary device (DWORD_00418f6c == 0) stored at 0x414a90\n  - Secondary device (DWORD_00418f6c == 1) stored at 0x414bb0\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x17c (380): DDCAPS structure size for DirectDraw7\n  0xe8 (232): DWORDs per device entry in data array\n  0x11: DDSCL_NORMAL cooperative level\n  0x20000: DDCAPS_BLT capability flag\n  0x100000: DDCAPS_BLTSTRETCH capability flag\n\nError Handling:\n  All DirectDraw COM method failures logged via FUN_00405370\n  Resources cleaned up in LAB_00404d90 exit path",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
