      "name": "RegisterDisplayMode",
      "signature": "uint RegisterDisplayMode(int * pSurfaceDesc, int * pContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Validates and registers a display mode for DirectDraw rendering.\nThis function is called during display mode enumeration to test and\nrecord valid display configurations for the graphics subsystem.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pContext is non-null; return 1 (success) if null\n2. Validate pSurfaceDesc is non-null and dwSize equals 0x6c\n3. Check mode count at pContext+0x39c does not exceed 0x1F (max 32 modes)\n4. Match bit depth at 640x480 resolution\n5. Look up corresponding bit mask from gdwBitMasks_exref table\n6. Call IDirectDraw::SetCooperativeLevel with DDSCL_EXCLUSIVE|DDSCL_FULLSCREEN\n7. Call IDirectDraw::SetDisplayMode with width, height, bpp\n8. Create primary surface with optional back buffer\n9. Store mode info at pContext+0x11c plus modeIndex times 0x14\n10. Increment mode counter at pContext+0x39c\n\nParameters:\npSurfaceDesc - Pointer to DDSURFACEDESC with mode info (dwSize=0x6c)\npContext - Display mode enumeration context structure\n\nReturns:\n1 - Success or skipped (unsupported mode)\n0 - Invalid parameters or exceeded max modes",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:13386bc2478665448e0627c4961b538f",
