      "name": "DetectGlideHardwareSupport",
      "signature": "dword DetectGlideHardwareSupport(HINSTANCE hInstance)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Detects and initializes 3dfx Glide hardware support for video rendering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Log detection message and load glide3x.dll\n2. If DLL missing, set no Glide support and return 0\n3. Retrieve all required Glide API function pointers (grGlideInit, grSstQueryBoards, grSstWinOpen, grSstWinClose, grTexMinAddress, grTexMaxAddress, grGet, grGlideShutdown, grSstSelect, grGetString)\n4. If any required function missing, log error and return 0\n5. Query number of Glide-compatible boards\n6. If no boards found, return 0\n7. Initialize Glide subsystem and select device 0\n8. Log hardware info (vendor, renderer, version)\n9. Create hidden enumeration window for Glide context\n10. Open Glide rendering context on window\n11. Query TMU (Texture Mapping Unit) count\n12. For each TMU, calculate available texture memory (max - min)\n13. Sum total texture memory from all TMUs\n14. If insufficient memory, cleanup and return 0\n15. Close Glide context, destroy window\n16. Copy \"3dfx Glide\" string to renderer name global\n17. Compare texture memory against threshold\n18. Return 2 if sufficient, 1 if insufficient\n\nParameters:\n  hInstance - HINSTANCE of the application module for window creation\n\nReturns:\n  0 - No Glide support (missing DLL, incomplete API, no boards, or failure)\n  1 - Glide supported but insufficient texture memory\n  2 - Glide fully supported with sufficient texture memory\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Uses SEH frame for exception safety during Glide operations\n  - Logs all detection steps for debugging\n  - Cleans up resources on any failure path\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x40000 - WS_EX_APPWINDOW extended window style\n  0x80000000 - WS_POPUP window style\n  0x280 (640) - Enumeration window width\n  0x1E0 (480) - Enumeration window height\n  0xF - GR_NUM_BOARDS Glide query constant\n  0x13 - GR_NUM_TMU Glide query constant\n  0xA1 - GR_HARDWARE Glide string constant\n  0xA2 - GR_RENDERER Glide string constant\n  0xA3 - GR_VENDOR Glide string constant\n  0xA4 - GR_VERSION Glide string constant\n  7 - GR_RESOLUTION_640x480 Glide resolution\n  2 - GR_REFRESH_60Hz Glide refresh rate",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04c",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:acbd5bf13cbc41aacaa4e3d2348b2786",
