      "name": "HandleFatalErrorAndExit",
      "signature": "void HandleFatalErrorAndExit(uint dwErrorCode)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Handles fatal application errors by logging and terminating the process.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if console display mode is enabled (g_dwConsoleDisplayFlag == 1)\n2. If enabled, call CleanupConsoleOutput() to flush/reset console state\n3. Write error message corresponding to dwErrorCode via WriteErrorMessage()\n4. Terminate process with exit code 0xFF (255) indicating fatal error\n\nParameters:\n  dwErrorCode (uint) - Error code identifying the specific fatal error condition\n\nReturns:\n  Does not return - terminates process via ExitProcess(0xFF)\n\nError Handling:\n  This IS the error handler - called when unrecoverable errors occur during startup\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xFF (255) - Process exit code indicating fatal error termination\n  0x1 - Console display mode flag value\n\nCalled From:\n  entry - Main entry point invokes this on critical initialization failures",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:439add363376dec04d1719690420901b838be92d80d5c4a09b514af1d3f8ed80",
