      "name": "ParseBindingFormatString",
      "signature": "int ParseBindingFormatString(void * this, int * param_1, byte * param_2, undefined4 * param_3)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Parse binding format string and extract numeric/string values from input buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize: Set output index (pbIndx) to zero, result counter (nResult) to zero\n2. Main loop: Process format string character by character\n   a. If current char is not '%', compare it with input data; advance on match\n   b. If '%' found, enter format specifier parsing mode\n3. Format specifier parsing: Handle modifiers after '%'\n   - '*' (0x2a): Width from argument, 'I' (0x49): 64-bit flag\n   - 'L' (0x4c): Long modifier, 'h' (0x68): Short modifier\n   - 'w' (0x77): Wide character modifier\n4. Parse width/precision: Accumulate decimal digits 0-9 (0x30-0x39)\n5. Format type dispatch: Switch on specifier character\n   - 'n' (0x6e): Store current format position\n   - 'c'/'C' (0x63/0x43): Single character with optional set\n   - 'd'/'i'/'u' (0x64/0x69/0x75): Decimal integer\n   - 'o' (0x6f): Octal integer (base 8)\n   - 'x' (0x78): Hexadecimal integer (base 16)\n   - 's' (0x73): String with charset validation\n   - 'p' (0x70): Pointer (long modifier)\n   - '{' (0x7b): Custom charset [chars] or [^chars]\n6. For character sets: Build 32-byte (256-bit) bitmap lookup table\n7. For integers: Accumulate digits using base multiplication (__allmul, __allshl)\n8. Process sign: Handle '+'/'-' (0x2b/0x2d) for signed integers\n9. Store results: Write parsed value to output array, increment counters\n10. Return: Compare format/input end positions, return count of matches\n\nParameters:\n  this (void*): Format context object (binding format structure)\n  szFormat (char*): Input format string containing % specifiers\n  pbData (byte*): Input data buffer to parse against format\n  pdwOutput (dword*): Array of dword pointers (2-4 slots for output values)\n\nReturns:\n  int: Number of successfully matched format specifiers (0 = parse failed or no matches)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Character sets: [characters] or [^excluded]; 32-byte bitmap for 0-255 range\n  - Width wildcard '*' (0x2a): Takes width from next format argument\n  - Precision modifier (0x2e): Maximum characters consumed for this specifier\n  - Sign preservation: Both '+' and '-' signs preserved during accumulation\n  - Exponential: 'e'/'E' (0x65) parsed for floating-point exponent chain\n  - 64-bit integers: Full 64-bit accumulation for I64/LL suffixes\n  - Binding context: Uses g_pBindingStates for state flag queries (0x80 mask)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
