      "name": "RewindBufferIfNotTerminal",
      "signature": "void RewindBufferIfNotTerminal(dword nByteValue, int * pBufferPos)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Rewind buffer position if byte value is not terminal marker (0xFFFFFFFF).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if nByteValue equals 0xFFFFFFFF (terminal sentinel)\n2. If NOT terminal, call processing function FUN_6fba202f\n3. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nnByteValue (dword) - Byte value to validate, 0xFFFFFFFF indicates end of stream\npBufferPos (int *) - Pointer to buffer position for format string parsing\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Always returns without error\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Terminal value 0xFFFFFFFF skips processing and returns immediately\n- Used in format string binding parsing to handle position advancement",
