      "name": "ProcessExceptionFrameChain",
      "signature": "void ProcessExceptionFrameChain(void * pHeadFrame, dword dwFrameFlags, void * pFrameList, int nStopIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Processes exception handler frame chain from current index to stop index.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save current exception context and establish SEH frame with mode flags\n2. Load current frame index from pHeadFrame at offset 0x8\n3. Loop while frame index != nStopIndex:\n   a. Validate frame index in bounds: 0 <= index < pFrameList.size (at pFrameList + 0x4)\n   b. Call exception error handler (FUN_6fb9c2d9) if bounds violated\n   c. Load frame handler from pFrameList array at (index * 8 + 4)\n   d. If handler present, invoke __CallSettingFrame with code 0x103\n   e. Advance frame index: index = pFrameList.array[index * 8]\n4. Store final frame index back to pHeadFrame offset 0x8\n5. Restore previous exception context\n6. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\npHeadFrame (void *) - Pointer to head of exception frame chain; offset +0x8 contains current frame index to process\ndwFrameFlags (dword) - Exception mode/state flags; stored in SEH context at FS:[0]\npFrameList (void *) - Array structure containing frame records; offset +0x4 is max frame count, offset +0x8 points to frame array\nnStopIndex (int) - Frame index to stop iteration at; loop terminates when current index equals this value\n\nReturns:\nvoid - None. Updates pHeadFrame->frame_index with final iteration value and restores exception context.",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:85c4fb6dc6180330f3c2b2e01bef37c2099c1b62d5b54e7e65fabb616b8194cd",
