      "name": "FilterCppException",
      "signature": "int FilterCppException(void * * ppExceptionPointers)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Exception filter that identifies and handles Microsoft C++ exceptions.\n\nThis function is used as an exception filter in structured exception handling (SEH).\nIt checks if the raised exception is a C++ exception by comparing the exception code\nagainst the Microsoft C++ exception magic number (0xE06D7363 = \"msc\\0\").\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Dereference ppExceptionPointers to get EXCEPTION_RECORD pointer\n2. Read the ExceptionCode from offset 0 of EXCEPTION_RECORD\n3. Compare ExceptionCode against 0xE06D7363 (Microsoft C++ signature)\n4. If NOT a C++ exception, return 0 (EXCEPTION_CONTINUE_SEARCH)\n5. If C++ exception, tail-call SetupStructuredExceptionHandler for processing\n\nParameters:\n  ppExceptionPointers - Pointer to EXCEPTION_POINTERS structure containing\n                        exception record and context information\n\nReturns:\n  0 - If exception is not a C++ exception (EXCEPTION_CONTINUE_SEARCH)\n  Result of SetupStructuredExceptionHandler - For C++ exceptions\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0xE06D7363 - Microsoft C++ exception signature (\"msc\\0\" encoded as little-endian)\n               Decompiler shows as -0x1F928C9D (two's complement representation)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
