      "name": "ReadByteFromBufferStream",
      "signature": "uint ReadByteFromBufferStream(uint * pStreamBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Read next byte from stream buffer, handling validation and property checks.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load stream flags from pStreamBuffer[3] (offset 0xC)\n2. Check if stream is active (flags & 0x83 != 0) and not in closed state (flags & 0x40 == 0)\n3. If not yet read-enabled (flags & 0x2 == 0):\n   a. Set read-enabled flag (0x1) on stream state\n   b. If stream not blocked (flags & 0x10C == 0), call FUN_6fba1db1 to initialize\n   c. Else copy buffer pointer from pStreamBuffer[2] to pStreamBuffer[0]\n4. Call ValidateAndProcessEntitySlot to validate buffer position and get remaining count\n5. Store result count in pStreamBuffer[1]\n6. If result valid (non-zero, not -1):\n   a. Check if stream property has flags 0x82 set, if so set property flag 0x2000\n   b. If buffer at position 0x200 and flags have 0x8 but not 0x400, update to 0x1000\n   c. Decrement result count and store back to pStreamBuffer[1]\n   d. Load byte from buffer pointer at pStreamBuffer[0], increment pointer\n   e. Return the byte value\n7. Else (error case):\n   a. Set error flags based on return value (0x10 or 0x20)\n   b. Zero out pStreamBuffer[1] count\n8. Return 0xFFFFFFFF if stream validation failed\n\nParameters:\npStreamBuffer (uint *): Pointer to stream control structure with fields at offsets 0-6:\n  [0] = data buffer pointer (byte *)\n  [1] = remaining count / result code (uint)\n  [2] = buffer start position (byte *)\n  [3] = stream flags (uint): bits 0x1=read-enabled, 0x2=read-pending, 0x8=position-check, 0x40=closed, 0x400=partial, 0x10C=blocked\n  [4] = stream property ID (uint, 0xFFFFFFFF for default)\n  [5] = reserved/internal\n  [6] = buffer position code (uint: 0x200 or 0x1000)\n\nReturns:\nuint: Next byte from stream (0x00-0xFF), or 0xFFFFFFFF if stream error/closed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns 0xFFFFFFFF if stream already closed (flags & 0x40) or validation failed\n- Returns 0xFFFFFFFF if property validation failed (FUN_6fba1db1 or result code -1)\n- Magic number 0x82: Property validation mask for state bits 1 and 7\n- Magic number 0x2000: Property indicator flag set on successful validation\n- Magic number 0x24: Property table entry stride (36 bytes per entry)\n- Magic number 0x1f: Property index bitmask (32 entries per table array slot)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
