      "name": "CheckArrayFirstThreeZero",
      "signature": "int CheckArrayFirstThreeZero(int * pnArray)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Checks whether the first three integers in an array are all zero.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize loop counter (nIndex) to 0\n2. Enter do-while loop for three iterations\n3. Check if current array element is non-zero\n4. If non-zero found, return 0 (false) immediately\n5. Increment loop counter and advance array pointer by 4 bytes\n6. Continue loop while counter < 3\n7. If all three elements are zero, return 1 (true)\n\nParameters:\n  pnArray - int * - Pointer to integer array to check (must have at least 3 elements)\n\nReturns:\n  1 - All first three elements are zero (validation passed)\n  0 - At least one of the first three elements is non-zero (validation failed)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Function assumes pnArray points to valid memory with at least 3 integers\n  No null pointer validation performed - caller must ensure valid array\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x3 (3) - Number of array elements to check\n  0x4 (4) - Size of int in bytes for pointer arithmetic",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:b6cef1f2da3c3f7439acaeabbf4ff6921e0941a9537b6fb2ed1c9a8155ea06d6",
