      "name": "ValidateStreamPropertyId",
      "signature": "void ValidateStreamPropertyId(uint dwPropertyId)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Validates a stream property ID and sets the corresponding DOS error code in TLS.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Store the property ID in the DOS errno TLS slot\n2. Search the property ID to error translation table for a matching entry\n3. If found, retrieve the corresponding DOS error code from the paired entry\n4. If not found, check for known property ID ranges:\n   - Range 0x13-0x24: Set error 0x0D (EINVAL - invalid data)\n   - Range 0xBC-0xCA: Set error 0x08 (ENOEXEC - exec format error)\n   - Default: Set error 0x16 (EINVAL - invalid argument)\n\nParameters:\n  dwPropertyId - Stream property ID to validate (passed via stack)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Error code is stored in TLS via GetTlsContextSlotPointer()\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x60028100 - g_adwStreamPropertyIdToErrorTable: Translation table base\n  0x60028268 - End of translation table (45 entries, 8 bytes each)\n  0x13-0x24  - Reserved property ID range (maps to EINVAL 0x0D)\n  0xBC-0xCA  - Extended property ID range (maps to ENOEXEC 0x08)\n  0x0D       - DOS error: EINVAL (invalid data)\n  0x08       - DOS error: ENOEXEC (exec format error)\n  0x16       - DOS error: EINVAL (invalid argument)\n\nStructure Layout (Translation Table Entry):\n  Offset  Size  Field       Type  Description\n  0x00    4     dwPropId    uint  Property ID to match\n  0x04    4     dwDosError  uint  Corresponding DOS error code",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:370daa173801763529aad9cbb097d7188d268733f7b18d543ff84e083c725b1f",
