      "name": "FindStructureByIdInArray",
      "signature": "dword FindStructureByIdInArray(int nSearchId, dword dwArrayBase)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Search array for structure with matching ID field\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize dwResultAddress to dwArrayBase\n2. Compare ID at offset +4 of first element (*(dwArrayBase + 4)) against nSearchId\n3. If match found on first try, skip loop and verify final result\n4. If not found, iterate through array:\n   - Calculate array upper bound: dwArrayBase + (g_dwStructureCount * 0xc)\n   - Advance dwResultAddress by 0xc bytes per iteration\n   - Check if reached array boundary (dwResultAddress >= upper bound)\n   - If not at boundary, compare ID at (dwResultAddress + 4) with nSearchId\n   - Continue until match found or boundary reached\n5. Final verification: Check both conditions:\n   - dwResultAddress is within array bounds\n   - ID at (dwResultAddress + 4) == nSearchId\n6. Return structure address if found, else return 0\n\nParameters:\nnSearchId (int) - ID to search for in structure array field at offset +4\ndwArrayBase (dword) - Base address of structure array (array of 12-byte elements)\n\nReturns:\ndword - Address of structure with matching ID (element base address), or 0 if not found\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x0    | 4    | field_00   | dword| Unknown field\n0x4    | 4    | nId        | int  | ID searched by this function\n0x8    | 4    | field_08   | dword| Unknown field\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If array is empty or first element doesn't match, fallback to linear search\n- If no match found after scanning all elements, returns 0\n- Magic number 0xc = structure size (12 bytes), used for stride calculation\n- Global g_dwStructureCount = number of elements in array",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:84a8c9e9d52af3dea832375d1b2499d5e6f4a7da784c988a8ffb9625c6ba83d3",
