      "name": "RunSplashDialogThread",
      "signature": "DWORD RunSplashDialogThread(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "DWORD",
      "comment": "Thread procedure for splash dialog window.\n\nCreates and displays a modeless splash dialog, then runs a standard\nWindows message loop to process dialog messages until the window is closed.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Create splash dialog using resource ID 0x68 with HandleSplashDialogProc\n2. Store dialog handle in global DWORD_00418068\n3. Show the dialog window (SW_SHOWNORMAL)\n4. Enter message loop:\n   a. Get next message from thread queue\n   b. Exit if WM_QUIT or dialog handle becomes NULL\n   c. Try IsDialogMessageA for dialog-specific processing\n   d. If not dialog message, translate and dispatch normally\n5. Return 0 (thread exit code)\n\nParameters:\n  lpParam (LPVOID) - Thread parameter (unused in this implementation)\n\nReturns:\n  DWORD - Always returns 0 on normal exit\n\nGlobals:\n  DWORD_00418068 - Splash dialog window handle (HWND)\n  DWORD_00415050 - Module instance handle (HINSTANCE)\n\nCalled From:\n  CreateThread lpStartAddress parameter\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Dialog can be closed externally by setting DWORD_00418068 to NULL\n  - Loop checks handle validity before AND after GetMessageA",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04c",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:9d4596c2ac5f600ab9e5d0c8b34876c5c6d1ed48ed53d2ba2872f1991d9ac4d1",
