      "name": "HandlePasswordDialogProc",
      "signature": "INT_PTR HandlePasswordDialogProc(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "INT_PTR",
      "comment": "Dialog procedure for the password entry dialog.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check message type (uMsg)\n2. If WM_COMMAND (0x111): End dialog with control ID from wParam\n3. If WM_INITDIALOG (0x110):\n   a. Get password edit control handle (ID 1000)\n   b. Load password prompt string (resource 5) into edit control text buffer\n   c. Load password info string (resource 0x27) into info buffer\n   d. Check if extra info is available via FUN_00401730\n   e. If available, append info string to prompt; else hide cancel button (ID 4)\n   f. Set window text for edit control and dialog title (resource 6)\n   g. Activate and bring dialog to foreground using multiple window APIs\n4. Return TRUE (1) for WM_INITDIALOG, FALSE (0) for other messages\n\nParameters:\n  hDlg   - HWND: Handle to the dialog window (stack offset 0x2108 after alloc)\n  uMsg   - UINT: Message identifier (stack offset 0x210c after alloc)\n  wParam - WPARAM: Message-specific parameter (stack offset 0x2110 after alloc)\n  lParam - LPARAM: Message-specific parameter (unused)\n\nReturns:\n  INT_PTR: TRUE (1) if WM_INITDIALOG handled, FALSE (0) otherwise\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x110  - WM_INITDIALOG message\n  0x111  - WM_COMMAND message\n  0x3e8  - Control ID 1000 (password edit control)\n  0x4    - Control ID 4 (cancel button)\n  0x2104 - Stack frame size allocated by prologue\n  SW_HIDE (0), SW_SHOW (1), SW_SHOW (5) - ShowWindow commands",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04c",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:20f7636e17f67d515574932a116e9610",
