      "name": "SetLanguageIdFromDisplayMode",
      "signature": "word SetLanguageIdFromDisplayMode(byte bDisplayModeIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "word",
      "comment": "Sets the active language ID and back buffer height from a display mode lookup table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate bDisplayModeIndex is less than 13 (0x0D)\n2. If valid, use index to lookup language ID from g_wDefaultLanguageId table (stride 8 bytes)\n3. Store language ID to g_wActiveLanguageId for localized resource loading\n4. Lookup and store screen dimensions to g_dwBackBufferHeight from g_dwScreenWidth table\n5. Return the newly set language ID\n6. If index >= 13, return current g_wActiveLanguageId unchanged\n\nParameters:\n- bDisplayModeIndex (CL): Display mode table index (0-12 valid range)\n\nReturns:\n- word: Active language ID (LANGID) after operation\n  - Valid index: Returns newly set language ID from table\n  - Invalid index (>=13): Returns current g_wActiveLanguageId unchanged\n\nDisplay Mode Table Layout (0x004139f8, stride 8 bytes per entry):\nOffset  Size  Field             Description\n0x00    2     wLanguageId       Windows LANGID (e.g., 0x0409 = English US)\n0x02    2     wPadding          Alignment padding\n0x04    4     dwScreenWidth     Screen width/height value for mode\n\nGlobals Modified:\n- g_wActiveLanguageId (0x00418fac): Set to table[index].wLanguageId\n- g_dwBackBufferHeight (0x00418fa8): Set to table[index].dwScreenWidth\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x0D (13): Maximum valid display mode index (exclusive bound)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- InitDefaultLanguageId: Resets language ID to default (index 0)\n- LoadLocalizedResourceA: Uses g_wActiveLanguageId with FindResourceExA\n- LoadLocalizedStringA: Uses g_dwBackBufferHeight for resource loading",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04c",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:e877a825a07e92fa154833623df3f945134af36a37e1760486ddd1ef5a0843a7",
