      "name": "LoadCursor",
      "signature": "HCURSOR LoadCursor(HINSTANCE hInstance, LPCSTR lpszCursorName)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Loads a cursor resource from the specified module.\n\nThin wrapper that directly calls the Windows API LoadCursorA to load a cursor\nresource by name from an application or DLL instance.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push lpszCursorName (EDX) onto stack\n2. Push hInstance (ECX) onto stack\n3. Call LoadCursorA via import table\n4. Return HCURSOR result from EAX\n\nParameters:\n  hInstance (HINSTANCE, ECX): Handle to the module containing the cursor resource.\n                              Pass NULL to load a standard system cursor.\n  lpszCursorName (LPCSTR, EDX): Cursor resource name or MAKEINTRESOURCE identifier.\n                                 For system cursors: IDC_ARROW, IDC_IBEAM, etc.\n\nReturns:\n  HCURSOR: Handle to the loaded cursor on success.\n           NULL on failure (call GetLastError for details).\n\nCallers:\n  RunVideoTest - Loads cursor during video test initialization",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:10a13a1aecaf2407b002fc09be7a8b619d2143e470d8c81e5545c94fa0ab8110",
