      "name": "LoadLocalizedStringA",
      "signature": "void LoadLocalizedStringA(HMODULE hModule, dword nStringId, LPSTR lpszBuffer, int nBufferSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Loads a localized string resource and converts it to ANSI.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate string table block index from string ID (nStringId >> 4) + 1\n2. Call FUN_004062b0 to find localized string table resource (RT_STRING = 6)\n3. If resource not found, fall back to LoadStringA\n4. Navigate to specific string entry within block using (nStringId & 0xF) index\n5. Convert wide-character string to multibyte using WideCharToMultiByte\n6. If conversion fails, fall back to LoadStringA\n7. Null-terminate the result buffer\n\nParameters:\n  hModule (HMODULE, ECX): Module handle containing string resources\n  nStringId (dword, EDX): String resource identifier\n  lpszBuffer (LPSTR, Stack+0x4): Output buffer for ANSI string\n  nBufferSize (int, Stack+0x8): Size of output buffer in characters\n\nReturns:\n  void - String copied to lpszBuffer on success\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Falls back to LoadStringA if localized resource not found\n  - Falls back to LoadStringA if WideCharToMultiByte fails\n  - Buffer is null-terminated after successful conversion\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  - 0x6: RT_STRING resource type for string tables\n  - 0xF: Mask to get string index within block (16 strings per block)\n  - 0x200: WC_NO_BEST_FIT_CHARS flag for WideCharToMultiByte\n  - >> 4: String tables contain 16 strings each, ID/16 gives block number",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04c",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:788f2b6e6d6f04669c0072e478e3df61c5fdcf2fc10dbcdf30be8105d7ad59a9",
