      "name": "InitializeLinkedListNode",
      "signature": "void InitializeLinkedListNode(uint * pNode)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initialize linked list node structure with self-referential pointers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load base pointer to node from ECX register (fastcall parameter)\n2. Calculate next node pointer offset (+0x4 bytes from base)\n3. Clear offset +0x4 (pNext field) to zero\n4. Clear offset +0x8 (pPrev field) to zero\n5. Set pNext field to point to itself (self-reference)\n6. Clear base offset (pFirst field) to zero\n7. Invert pNext pointer and store in pPrev field (inverted self-reference)\n8. Return\n\nParameters:\npNode (uint *) - IMPLICIT in ECX: pointer to linked list node structure (size 0xC bytes minimum)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Structure initialized in-place at pNode\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x0    | 4    | pFirst     | uint*| First node pointer (cleared to 0)\n0x4    | 4    | pNext      | uint*| Next node pointer (set to self)\n0x8    | 4    | pPrev      | uint*| Previous node pointer (inverted self-reference)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x4 - Offset to pNext field (second dword)\n0x8 - Offset to pPrev field (third dword)\n\nNote: Function uses 1 stack-allocated temporary optimized away by compiler (visible only in disassembly as EDX register)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04c",
