      "name": "UnlinkAndClearListNodes",
      "signature": "void UnlinkAndClearListNodes(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Unlinks and clears all nodes in a doubly-linked list container.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load node count from container structure at offset +0x8\n2. If count <= 0, exit immediately (empty or invalid list)\n3. Load base pointer from container at offset +0x0\n4. Begin iteration loop while count > 0\n5. Load node value from memory at (basePtr + count offset)\n6. Calculate node address as (basePtr + count)\n7. If node value is zero, skip to next iteration\n8. Load successor offset from node address + 0x4\n9. Determine target pointer based on successor offset sign bit\n10. If successor offset is negative: use bitwise NOT to recover pointer address\n11. If successor offset is positive: calculate target as (nodeAddr + offset - node[+4])\n12. Store original node value at calculated target pointer address\n13. Load forward pointer from current node address +0x0\n14. Load successor offset again from node address +0x4\n15. Update forward pointer's successor link by storing offset at (forwardPtr + 0x4)\n16. Clear node's forward pointer field (set to 0)\n17. Clear node's successor offset field (set to 0)\n18. Loop decrements count and continues to next node\n19. Return when count reaches 0\n\nParameters:\n  pListContainer: Pointer to container structure holding linked list metadata\n    Structure layout at pListContainer:\n      +0x0: basePtr (void*) - Base pointer to node array in memory\n      +0x8: nodeCount (int) - Active node count (decremented during iteration)\n  \n  IMPLICIT pContainerEDI: Actual container pointer passed via EDI register\n    This function uses a custom calling convention where EDI holds the real container\n    The stack parameter pListContainer is not actually used in the function body\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value, modifies linked list structure in-place by unlinking all nodes\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Negative successor offset: Uses two's complement bitwise NOT (~offset) to recover actual pointer address\n  - Positive successor offset: Requires complex calculation (nodeAddr + offset - node.successor)\n  - Zero node value: Skipped without processing to handle uninitialized or deleted nodes\n  - Count modification: Container's count field is decremented during iteration\n  - Forward and successor pointers: Both cleared to 0 after unlinking each node\n\nStructure Layout:\nContainer Structure (12 bytes):\n  Offset | Size | Field Name  | Type  | Description\n  -------|------|-------------|-------|----------------------------------\n  +0x00  | 4    | basePtr     | void* | Base pointer to node array\n  +0x08  | 4    | nodeCount   | int   | Active node count\n\nNode Structure (12 bytes):\n  Offset | Size | Field Name   | Type | Description\n  -------|------|--------------|------|----------------------------------\n  +0x00  | 4    | forwardPtr   | int* | Link to forward node or NULL\n  +0x04  | 4    | successorOff | int  | Successor pointer (may be encoded)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
