      "name": "HandleSplashDialogProc",
      "signature": "dword HandleSplashDialogProc(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Dialog procedure callback for the splash/initialization dialog.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x1100 bytes of stack space for string buffers\n2. Check message type (uMsg):\n   - WM_INITDIALOG (0x110): Initialize dialog UI\n   - Close command (0x4C9): End dialog and return result\n   - Other: Return 0 (not handled)\n3. For WM_INITDIALOG:\n   a. Get handle to static text control (ID 0x3F8)\n   b. Load resource string 0x15 into 0x1000-byte buffer\n   c. Set static text control with loaded string\n   d. Show static text control\n   e. Load resource string 0x14 into 0x100-byte buffer\n   f. Set dialog title with loaded string\n   g. Show dialog window\n   h. Return 1 (TRUE) to indicate handled\n4. For close command (0x4C9):\n   a. Call EndDialog with low word of lParam as result\n   b. Clear global dialog handle (g_hSplashDialog)\n   c. Return 0\n\nParameters:\n  hDlg (HWND): Handle to the dialog window\n  uMsg (UINT): Message identifier\n  wParam (WPARAM): Additional message-specific information\n  lParam (LPARAM): Additional message-specific information\n\nReturns:\n  1 (TRUE): WM_INITDIALOG handled successfully\n  0 (FALSE): Message not handled or close command processed\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x110 = WM_INITDIALOG - Dialog initialization message\n  0x4C9 = Custom close command message ID\n  0x3F8 = Control ID for static text control (resource ID 1016)\n  0x15 = Resource string ID 21 - splash text content\n  0x14 = Resource string ID 20 - dialog title\n  0x1000 = 4096-byte buffer for splash text\n  0x100 = 256-byte buffer for title text\n\nGlobals:\n  DWORD_00418068 = g_hSplashDialog - Handle to splash dialog window\n  DWORD_00415050 = g_hInstance - Module instance handle for resources",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.10",
