      "name": "ScanfFormatStringParser",
      "signature": "undefined ScanfFormatStringParser(FILE * pFile, byte * pFormatString, void * * pArguments)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Parse formatted input from file stream according to format string specification (scanf-style).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize SEH frame and validate stack cookie for buffer overflow protection\n2. Main format parsing loop: iterate through each character in format string\n3. For whitespace characters: skip all whitespace in input stream\n4. For '%' format specifier: parse complete format specification\n   a. Parse width specifier: digit sequence or '*' (suppress assignment)\n   b. Parse size modifiers: 'h' (short/2), 'l'/'w' (long/4), 'I64' (64-bit/8)\n   c. Parse conversion type character: d/i/o/x/u (integer), f/e/g (float), c (char), s (string), '[' (scanset), n (count), p (pointer)\n5. For integer formats (d,i,o,x,u,p): parse optional sign, handle prefixes (0x for hex, 0 for octal), accumulate digits\n6. For floating formats (f,e,g): parse sign, digits, decimal point, exponent notation\n7. For character format 'c': read width characters (default 1), convert multibyte if wide modifier\n8. For string format 's': read until whitespace, null-terminate result\n9. For scanset format '[abc]': build character bitmap, read matching characters until no match\n10. For 'n' format: store count of consumed characters\n11. For literal characters: match exact input or fail format\n12. Skip whitespace between format specs unless '%c' or '[' format\n13. Increment conversion count on successful assignment (except for '*' and 'n')\n14. Return conversion count or -1 if EOF before any conversions\n\nParameters:\n  pFile - FILE pointer for input stream\n  pFormatString - Format string with conversion specifications (% delimited)\n  pArguments - Array of pointers to argument output locations\n\nReturns:\n  int - Number of successfully assigned input items (conversion count), or -1 (EOF) if no input\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Width '*' - Suppress assignment flag (data consumed but not stored)\n  64-bit I64 modifier - Extended double-word integer format\n  Hex prefix - 0x or 0X forces base-16 interpretation\n  Octal prefix - 0 forces base-8 interpretation\n  Character class - Bitmap with 32 bytes (256 bits) for fast matching\n  Multibyte conversion - Uses locale-aware character type table\n  Decimal point - Locale-specific separator from g_byLocaleDecimalPoint\n  EOF handling - Returns -1 only if no conversions made before EOF\n\nGlobal Dependencies:\n  g_dwSecurityCookie - Stack canary for overflow detection\n  g_byLocaleDecimalPoint - Locale decimal separator (typically '.')\n  g_pCharTypeTable - Character type/classification table\n  g_pfnFloatAssign - Function pointer for float string-to-value conversion\n  g_dwLocaleMaxMBCharSize - Maximum multibyte character size for locale",
