      "name": "ReadTextFile",
      "signature": "int ReadTextFile(uint fileDescriptorIndex, char * outputBuffer, uint bufferSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Reads text data from a file descriptor with automatic CR/LF line-ending conversion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input buffer size is non-zero; return 0 if invalid\n2. Extract file descriptor index: bucket = (index >> 5), stride = (index & 0x1f) * 0x24\n3. Load file descriptor entry flags at offset +0x04 to check if file is closed (0x02)\n4. Check for buffered character (flags 0x48); copy buffered char to output if not newline\n5. Call ReadFile Windows API to read raw bytes from file handle into output buffer\n6. Handle read errors: error 5 (ACCESS_DENIED) maps to errno 9, error 0x6D returns 0 silently\n7. If binary mode (0x80), return bytes read immediately without conversion\n8. If text mode, scan buffer for CR/LF sequences, EOF markers (0x1A), and normalize line endings\n9. Set eof_reached flag (0x04) if first char is newline (CR+LF continuation from previous read)\n10. Process each character: regular chars copied as-is, CR/LF converted, EOF (0x1A) terminates read\n11. Return total characters written to output buffer after conversion\n\nParameters:\nfileDescriptorIndex (uint) - Index into file descriptor array, scaled by 36 bytes per entry\noutputBuffer (char*) - Destination buffer for converted text data\nbufferSize (uint) - Maximum bytes to read and convert\n\nReturns:\n0 - Buffer size is zero or file is closed\n-1 - ReadFile error occurred (errno set by error handler)\n>0 - Number of bytes written to output buffer after line-ending conversion\n\nFile Descriptor Structure (0x24 / 36 bytes stride):\nOffset  Size  Field          Type       Description\n+0x00   4     handle         HANDLE     Windows file handle for I/O operations\n+0x04   1     flags          byte       Status and mode flags (bit-packed)\n+0x05   1     buffered       char       Buffered character from lookahead read\n+0x06   30    [other]        varies     Additional descriptor fields\n\nFlag Bits (offset +0x04):\n0x02 - File closed (handle invalid)\n0x04 - EOF reached (newline detected after CR+LF)\n0x08 - Has buffered character from lookahead (combined with 0x40)\n0x40 - EOF marker seen (Ctrl+Z / 0x1A detected)\n0x80 - Binary mode (skip all line-ending conversion)\n\nCR/LF Conversion State Machine:\nState CR+LF: Output single LF, consume both, advance position by 2\nState CR@boundary: ReadFile 1 byte lookahead, output LF if lookahead==LF else save lookahead\nState Lone CR: Output CR character unchanged\nState EOF (0x1A): Set EOF marker flag, terminate conversion\nState Regular: Copy character to output unchanged\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Buffered char (flags 0x48): Copy to output first if not newline\n- Binary mode (0x80): Skip conversion, return immediately after ReadFile\n- CR at buffer boundary: Perform lookahead read to detect CR+LF sequence\n- EOF marker (0x1A): Terminates read, sets eof_marker_seen flag (0x40)\n- Access denied (error 5): Maps to errno 9 (EBADF), DOS errno 5\n- Broken pipe (error 0x6D): Returns 0 silently (EOF condition)\n- Seek back: When CR at boundary not followed by LF, rewinds file position by 1 byte\n\nImplementation Notes:\n- bufferSize parameter is reused as read pointer after ReadFile call\n- Original size value no longer needed, so parameter repurposed to save stack space\n- Uses 36-byte descriptor stride (9 DWORDs) for file handle array indexing\n- Supports text/binary mode flags for selective line-ending conversion\n- Implements lookahead buffer mechanism for CR+LF boundary detection",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.12a",
