      "name": "DetectOsAndValidateDirectX",
      "signature": "bool DetectOsAndValidateDirectX(DWORD dwDisposition, int nMajorVersion, int nMinorVersion, DWORD dwDataSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Detects the operating system version and validates DirectX installation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize SEH frame and allocate stack space\n2. Get fog state pointer containing OS information\n3. Log detection start message and set detection state to 2 (detecting)\n4. Check OS type from fog state structure (offset +4)\n5. For NT 4.0 with specific version range, auto-pass without registry check\n6. For Win95/98/NT/2K (types 1-4), open DirectX registry key\n7. Query DirectX version string from HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\DirectX\n8. Parse version string as \"%d.%d.%d.%d\" format\n9. Validate: major >= 5, or major == 4 with minor >= 7\n10. If invalid, show message box prompting user action (IDYES=6 to proceed)\n11. Update global detection state: 0=valid, 1=invalid, 2=detecting\n12. Close registry key and restore exception handler\n13. Return true if DirectX valid or user chose to proceed\n\nParameters:\n  dwDisposition (DWORD) - Repurposed: registry disposition output, then version type\n  nMajorVersion (int) - Repurposed: parsed DirectX major version number\n  nMinorVersion (int) - Repurposed: parsed DirectX minor version number  \n  dwDataSize (DWORD) - Repurposed: registry value buffer size (0x104 bytes)\n\nReturns:\n  true - DirectX installation is valid or user elected to proceed\n  false - DirectX installation failed validation and user declined\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  NT 4.0 specific version (float range check) - Auto-passes without registry check\n  Unknown OS type - Logs error, returns false\n  Missing registry key - Logs error, returns false\n  Missing version value - Logs error, returns false\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x80000002 - HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\n  0x1 - KEY_QUERY_VALUE registry access\n  0x104 - MAX_PATH buffer size\n  0x4 - MB_YESNO message box style\n  0x6 - IDYES message box result\n  0xe (14) - Resource ID for error message text\n  0xf (15) - Resource ID for error caption\n\nOS Type Values (from fog state +4):\n  1 - Windows 95\n  2 - Windows 98\n  3 - Windows NT\n  4 - Windows 2000/XP\n\nGlobal State (DWORD_00416058):\n  0 - DirectX valid\n  1 - DirectX invalid\n  2 - Detection in progress",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
