      "name": "HandleFinalVideoDialogProc",
      "signature": "INT_PTR HandleFinalVideoDialogProc(HWND hDlg, UINT uMsg, WPARAM wParam, LPARAM lParam)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "INT_PTR",
      "comment": "Dialog procedure for the final video mode selection dialog.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Handle WM_INITDIALOG (0x110):\n   a. Load dialog strings from resources\n   b. Set dialog title and description text\n   c. For each video mode (DirectDraw0, DirectDraw1, Direct3D0, Direct3D1, Glide):\n      - Set button label text\n      - Hide button if mode unavailable (state == 0)\n      - Auto-select button if mode recommended (state == 2)\n   d. If all modes unavailable, display failure message\n   e. Otherwise display info message with recommendations\n   f. Bring dialog to foreground and set focus\n2. Handle WM_COMMAND (0x111) with IDOK (wParam == 1):\n   a. Iterate through 5 video mode states\n   b. For each recommended mode (state == 2), call selection handler\n   c. Query each radio button checked state via BM_GETCHECK (0xF2)\n   d. Call FUN_004012f0 for any checked button\n   e. End dialog with IDOK result\n\nParameters:\n  hDlg    - Dialog window handle\n  uMsg    - Message identifier (WM_INITDIALOG or WM_COMMAND)\n  wParam  - Command identifier (IDOK=1 for WM_COMMAND)\n  lParam  - Additional message data (unused)\n\nReturns:\n  1 (TRUE)  - Message was processed\n  0 (FALSE) - Message was not processed\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x110  - WM_INITDIALOG\n  0x111  - WM_COMMAND\n  0xF2   - BM_GETCHECK (query button check state)\n  0xF5   - BM_SETCHECK (set button check state)\n  0x3ee  - IDC_RADIO_DDRAW0 (DirectDraw primary)\n  0x3ef  - IDC_RADIO_D3D0 (Direct3D primary)\n  0x3f0  - IDC_RADIO_GLIDE (3dfx Glide)\n  0x3f1  - IDC_RADIO_DDRAW1 (DirectDraw secondary)\n  0x3f2  - IDC_RADIO_D3D1 (Direct3D secondary)\n  0x3f3  - IDC_STATIC_INFO (info text control)\n  0x3f4  - IDC_STATIC_RECOMMEND (recommendation text)\n  0x3fd  - IDC_STATIC_DESC (description text)\n\nGlobal State Variables:\n  DWORD_00414bac - DirectDraw0 mode state (0=unavail, 1=avail, 2=recommended)\n  DWORD_00414ccc - DirectDraw1 mode state\n  DWORD_00414dec - Direct3D0 mode state\n  DWORD_00414f0c - Direct3D1 mode state\n  DWORD_0041502c - Glide mode state\n  DWORD_00415050 - Resource module handle\n  DWORD_00416058 - Error type for failure message selection",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:f00a56953e3fb0a6231a40b3d3f02b68",
