      "name": "RunVideoTest",
      "signature": "int RunVideoTest(HMODULE hInstance, dword dwUnused, LPCSTR lpszCmdLine)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Main entry point for D2VidTst.exe - Diablo II Video Test utility.\n\nDetects and tests graphics rendering capabilities (DirectDraw, Direct3D, Glide)\nthen writes configuration results to the Windows registry for the game to use.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Open d2data.mpq and read locale configuration from data\\local\\use file\n2. Check for existing instance via named event \"D2VideoTest\" (0xB7 = already exists)\n3. Initialize Fog library for logging subsystem\n4. Clear global video mode detection state arrays\n5. Access registry key SOFTWARE\\Blizzard Entertainment\\Diablo II\\VideoConfig\n6. Delete VidTestRequired flag if exists (indicates test completed)\n7. Display initial dialog (resource 0x65) - user selects test mode\n8. If user selects \"Configure Only\" (result=4), show config dialog and exit\n9. Check previous test crash markers (TestDDraw, TestD3D, TestGLIDE registry values)\n10. Enumerate display settings via EnumDisplaySettingsA (require 8+ bpp)\n11. Spawn progress dialog thread, wait up to 10 seconds for display\n12. Detect operating system compatibility via DetectOsAndValidateDirectX\n13. Register window class \"Enumeration_Class\" for DirectX testing\n14. Initialize video adapter info structures (0x414a90 to 0x415030)\n15. Run DirectDraw detection phase - mark registry before/after for crash recovery\n16. Run Direct3D detection phase with same crash protection pattern\n17. Run Glide (3dfx) detection phase with same crash protection pattern\n18. Display final configuration dialog (resource 0x66) for user selection\n19. Delete VidTestRequired flag and close registry on completion\n\nParameters:\n- hInstance (HMODULE): Application instance handle passed from WinMain\n- dwUnused (dword): Reserved parameter, unused by this function\n- lpszCmdLine (LPCSTR): Command line string, may contain video mode override value\n\nReturns:\n-  0: Success - video test completed normally\n- -1: User cancelled test or critical error occurred\n- Other: MessageBoxA result when already-running instance detected\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- ERROR_ALREADY_EXISTS (0xB7): Shows \"Already running\" message, exits gracefully\n- Display bits < 8: Shows warning dialog, allows user to cancel (returns -1)\n- RegisterClassA fails: Calls DisplayGfxError, may trigger INT3 debug breakpoint\n- OS detection fails: Skips detection phases, jumps directly to final dialog\n\nError Handling:\n- Registry operations wrapped with status checks, log on failure\n- Crash recovery via registry markers (TestDDraw/TestD3D/TestGLIDE set to 1=testing, 2=passed)\n- Dialog displays warning if previous test crashed (marker stuck at 1)\n\nDecompiler Notes:\n- extraout_var* variables are Ghidra artifacts for functions returning bool in AL\n  (upper 3 bytes of EAX are undefined when bool returned in AL) - cannot be typed\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0xB7 (183): ERROR_ALREADY_EXISTS from GetLastError\n- 0xF003F: KEY_ALL_ACCESS for registry operations\n- 0x80000001: HKEY_CURRENT_USER registry hive\n- 0x65 (101): IDD_INITIAL_DIALOG - Initial test selection dialog resource ID\n- 0x66 (102): IDD_CONFIG_DIALOG - Final configuration dialog resource ID\n- 0x69 (105): IDD_CRASH_WARNING_DIALOG - Crash recovery warning dialog resource ID\n- 0x7F00: IDC_ARROW cursor resource\n- 0x7F02: IDC_WAIT cursor resource\n- 0x4C9 (1225): WM_APP+0xC9 - Custom message to close progress dialog\n- 0x1000 (4096): MB_SYSTEMMODAL for message box flags\n- 0x3E8 (1000): 1 second delay in milliseconds\n- 0x7D0 (2000): 2 second delay between detection phases\n\nRegistry Keys Used:\n- SOFTWARE\\Blizzard Entertainment\\Diablo II\\VideoConfig\n- Values: VidTestRequired, TestDDraw, TestD3D, TestGLIDE\n\nStructure Layout (Video Adapter Array @ 0x414a90):\nOffset  Size  Field        Description\n0x00    4     dwFlags      Adapter capability flags\n0x04    4     dwField04    Unknown field 1\n0x08    4     dwField08    Unknown field 2\n0x0C    4     dwField0C    Unknown field 3\n0x10    4     dwField10    Unknown field 4\n0x14    4     dwField14    Unknown field 5\n0x18    4     dwField18    Unknown field 6\n0x1C    256   szName       Adapter name string (copied from 0x41807c)\nTotal: 0x120 (288) bytes per entry, array spans to 0x415030",
