      "name": "EnumerateDisplayAdapter",
      "signature": "dword EnumerateDisplayAdapter(dword * pGuidData, dword dwFlags, char * szDeviceName)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Enumerates and validates a DirectDraw/Direct3D display adapter for Diablo II compatibility.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize exception handler and clear adapter data structure\n2. Check maximum display count limit (max 2 adapters supported)\n3. Store GUID data if provided, otherwise set default display flag\n4. Create DirectDraw object via DirectDrawCreate\n5. Get DirectDraw4 interface via QueryInterface\n6. Retrieve device identifier to get Vendor/Device IDs\n7. Check for known incompatible hardware (Intel i740, Cirrus Logic 5xxx, SiS 530, etc.)\n8. Get D3D interface and set cooperative level\n9. Enumerate display modes and check for required 16-bit/32-bit support\n10. Create primary surface with backbuffer\n11. Query DirectDraw capabilities (gamma control, 3D support)\n12. Create D3D device and get device capabilities\n13. Verify texture requirements (video memory textures, triangles, mipmapping)\n14. Query video memory, texture memory, local memory, and AGP memory\n15. Check minimum 6MB free texture memory requirement\n16. Enumerate texture formats and verify 1555 texture support\n17. Store adapter info to primary or secondary display data structure\n18. Cleanup all COM interfaces on exit\n\nParameters:\n    pGuidData - Pointer to 16-byte GUID structure for adapter, or NULL for primary display\n    dwFlags - Display enumeration flags (unused in this implementation)\n    szDeviceName - Device name string to copy, or NULL to use queried description\n\nReturns:\n    0 - Exceeded maximum display count (already have 2 adapters)\n    1 - Adapter enumeration failed or cleanup completed\n    Result of FUN_004041c4 - Adapter successfully enumerated\n\nKnown Incompatible Hardware (Vendor:Device):\n    0x8086:0x7800 - Intel i740\n    0x1013:0x00D6 - Cirrus Logic 5xxx\n    0x1039:0x6306 - SiS 530\n    0x104C:0x3D07 - FireGL 1000 Pro\n    0x121A:0x0001-0x0005 - 3Dfx Voodoo series\n    0x1142:0x643D - Trident\n    0x10D9:0x8626 - Unknown (treated as 3Dfx)\n    0x1002:0x4755 - ATI Rage II\n\nCapability Flags Checked:\n    0x00020000 - DDCAPS2_CANRENDERWINDOWED (gamma control)\n    0x00100000 - DDCAPS2_CANCALIBRATEGAMMA\n    0x00000200 - D3DDEVCAPS_TEXTUREVIDEOMEMORY\n    0x00001000 - D3DDEVCAPS_DRAWPRIMITIVESINCURRENTPRIMITIVE\n    0x00000100 - D3DPTEXTURECAPS_POW2 (non-power-of-two textures)\n    0x00000040 - D3DPTFILTERCAPS_LINEARMIPNEAREST (triangle support)\n    0x00000020 - D3DPTEXTURECAPS_SQUAREONLY\n    0x00000020 - Mipmapping support\n\nMemory Requirements:\n    Minimum 6MB free texture memory (0x600000 bytes)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
