      "name": "CloseAndDeallocateStreamStructures",
      "signature": "int CloseAndDeallocateStreamStructures(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Closes all open stream files and deallocates dynamic stream structures.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire critical section 2 for thread-safe stream table access\n2. Iterate through stream structure table starting at index 3\n3. For each non-null stream structure:\n   a. If status flags (offset 0xC) have bits 0x83 set, close the file\n   b. Track successful file closes in return counter\n   c. If index >= 20 (0x14), this is a dynamic stream:\n      - Delete the embedded critical section at offset 0x20\n      - Deallocate the stream structure memory\n      - Clear the table entry\n4. Release critical section 2\n5. Return count of files successfully closed\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  int - Number of files successfully closed (via ThreadSafeFileClose)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x83 - Stream status flags mask (offset 0xC in structure)\n  0x20 - Offset of embedded CRITICAL_SECTION in stream structure\n  3    - First user stream index (indices 0-2 are reserved/system streams)\n  20   - Threshold for dynamic stream deallocation (indices >= 20 are dynamically allocated)\n\nStructure Layout (StreamStructure):\n  Offset  Size  Field               Type               Description\n  0x00    4     pFileHandle         int*               File handle/pointer\n  0x0C    1     bStatusFlags        byte               Status flags (0x83 mask = closeable)\n  0x20    24    criticalSection     CRITICAL_SECTION   Embedded critical section for thread safety\n\nNotes:\n  - Reserved streams (indices 0-2) are never closed or deallocated here\n  - Static streams (indices 3-19) have files closed but structures are not deallocated\n  - Dynamic streams (indices 20+) are fully cleaned up including memory deallocation\n  - Critical section index 2 protects the global stream structure table",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
